# data file for the Fltk User Interface Designer (fluid)
version 1.0500
header_name {.h}
code_name {.cxx}
comment {One row of "label, text field, browse button", the shape repeated all over
the Misc window. The label text and what the browse button does are supplied
per instance from Haskell (Onyx.GUI.Core.filePickerRow), so the label here is
only a placeholder for the editor.

Designed at 900x50, the width of a Misc tab, so placement there is a pure
translation. The input is the resizable child, so the browse button keeps its
width and stays pinned to the right edge at other sizes.} {in_source not_in_header
}

widget_class FilePickerRow {open
  xywh {0 0 900 50}
} {
  Fl_Input input {
    label File
    xywh {120 5 715 35} align 4 labelsize 13 resizable
  }
  Fl_Button pick {
    label {@fileopen}
    xywh {846 5 44 35}
  }
  code {// FLUID builds the children at their design coordinates, which assume this
// group sits at the origin at its design size. Restate that, then resize
// into the frame we were actually constructed with. Keep the numbers below
// in step with the xywh of the widget_class itself.
Fl_Widget::resize(0, 0, 900, 50);
resize(X, Y, W, H);} {}
}
